Dear [redacted], 

This is to acknowledge receipt of your Access to Information Act (Act) request received on April 13, 2026, for:

Records (briefing notes, legal opinions, risk assessments and human rights assessments and senior-level correspondence) from ADM(Pol), JAG, VCDS, CJOC and RCN, regarding Canada–Republic of Korea military cooperation and associated
 legal, policy, and human rights considerations in the context of Article 92-6 of the Republic of Korea’s Military Criminal Act, from January 1, 2024 to April 11, 2026, to include:

1.      Canada–Republic of Korea joint military exercises planned, conducted, or in preparation for May–June 2026, including associated naval activities such as port visits (including the planned docking of ROKS Dosan Ahn Chang-ho
 at HMCS Esquimalt)

2.      Legal, policy, human rights, or risk assessments relating to Article 92-6 of the Republic of Korea’s Military Criminal Act, which criminalizes consensual same-sex conduct between Korean military personnel

3.      Records addressing the implications or compatibility of Article 92-6 with Canadian legal and policy frameworks, including the Canadian Human Rights Act and applicable DND/CAF policies on harassment, sexual misconduct,
 and workplace inclusion

4.      Records addressing personnel policy or operational implications for CAF members participating in, embedded with, or training alongside Republic of Korea Navy forces

5.      Legal or policy analysis concerning Canada’s long-term naval cooperation obligation with the Republic of Korea (including the Canadian Patrol Submarine Project), where such analysis relates to personnel integration,
 exchanges, training, or interoperability in the context of Article 92-6.

Please use these keywords only in the context of Canada–Republic of Korea military cooperation/ Article 92-6 and not as standalone search terms: "Korean Military Criminal Act"; "ROKS Dosan Ahn Chang-ho"; "KSS-III"; "Esquimalt";
 "Canada-Korea exercises"; "sexual orientation"; "LGBTQ"; "homosexual"; "gay"; "CAF human rights"; "Hanwha Ocean"; "CPSP"; "Canadian Patrol Submarine Project"; "joint exercises Korea"; "personnel exchange Korea".

Please note that every effort is being made to process your request within the prescribed 30-day time limit pursuant to the Act. In addition, your request will be processed in accordance with the Principles for Assisting Requesters as per the Treasury Board
 Secretariat's policies and guidance which can be found at: 
https://www.canada.ca/en/treasury-board-secretariat/services/access-information-privacy/access-information/supporting-tool-access-information-personal-information-requests-principles-assisting-requesters.html.

Please be advised that the response to your request will be sent to you through Connect (https://www.canadapost-postescanada.ca/cpc/en/business/postal-services/digital-mail/connect.page).
 A portable document format (PDF) of the records will be uploaded to and will remain available for viewing in the Connect portal for 60 days.

For any questions concerning your request or if you wish to opt-out of Connect and obtain a copy of your records via regular mail, please contact our office by email at atip-aiprp@forces.gc.ca.

